; ============================================================================
; x.1sav.rtc - a clock reading normalized to a Unix instant
;
; An extension key for the Universal Saves Format, defined by these
; specifications under a name reserved in the Vendor Names registry because the
; value belongs to no single producer.
;
; The root here is the value carried under the key, not a bundle. A bundle
; validates against the format's own schema whatever this holds, since an
; extension value is `any` there; this file is what makes the shape checkable.
; ============================================================================

rtc = {
  0 => reading-seconds, ; reading     - what the clock shows, as a Unix instant
  ? 1 => uint,          ; accuracy_ms - uncertainty, in milliseconds
}

; Which clock produced the reading is not carried here. The chip key beside this
; one names it, `source` names the producer, and a normalized instant is meant
; to be readable without either.
;
; Key 0 is what the clock shows, never the point a counting clock advances from.
; An MBC3 footer's host timestamp is such an anchor; the reading is that plus
; the elapsed time the footer's counters describe.
;
; Tag 1 admits a float and this key does not, for the reason `created_at` gives
; in the format spec: one instant would otherwise have two encodings.
reading-seconds = #6.1(int)
